WEBVTT

00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:06,100
Hello, everybody. This is Dr. Kevin Connors. Just answering some of your questions.

00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:13,100
Here's a great question that came in. My body has been fighting the tumors with natural support.

00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:21,100
Tumors have been unofficially shrinking by examine and unofficially and my unofficial imaging.

00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:26,100
And I'm convinced that the tumors are also getting closer to the surface of my skin,

00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:32,100
and away from my body cavity, this person has a breast cancer.

00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:38,100
Sometimes the skin is in the areas hot and red and sometimes slightly bluish-tinned.

00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,100
These seem to coincide with good responses.

00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,100
I understand this moving to the skin is a good thing.

00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:50,100
However, my oncologist is fearful of this telling me that it gets in my skin and can spread all over my body.

00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:54,100
Please help me understand why I should not be afraid of the tumor.

00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:59,100
Moving towards the skin and breaking through the skin.

00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:07,100
So first of all, just so we clarify things, all statistics show that when a tumor, especially a breast cancer,

00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:10,100
is moving towards the skin, that's a good thing.

00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:18,100
It's when it moves towards the chest wall that would be considered a bad thing.

00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:22,100
So when it moves towards the chest wall, it adheres to the chest wall.

00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:30,100
It has the chance of a testicizing into the chest cavity, into the lung, into the liver.

00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:33,100
When it's a moving towards the surface, that's always a good thing.

00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:38,100
So why your oncologist would say that he's fearful of it moving towards the surface is beyond me,

00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,100
because there's no evidence of that.

00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:46,100
They probably give you a fear, scare if it was no matter which way it was moving.

00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:51,100
So that's just kind of the way things roll in those offices.

00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:57,100
So when there's a red response, that's typically a response of inflammation, that's a good thing.

00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:03,100
So you say, oh, inflammation is bad, but no, when you're firing in immune response to something, that's inflammatory.

00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:09,100
So there's acute inflammatory responses of an immune response to a cancer is a good thing.

00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:13,100
And it could actually cause a subtle enlargement of the tumor.

00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:18,100
It could make it look larger, because there's some inflammatory response around that cancer.

00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,100
So don't be fooled about that.

00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:25,100
So it's very good that it appears by palpation that is shrinking,

00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:30,100
that it appears by maybe thermography and ultrasonic things that it's shrinking.

00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,100
Those are very good things.

00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:35,100
And it's a very good thing that it's moving towards the skin.

00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,100
But I do want to make a comment in this last part.

00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:41,100
Please help me understand why I should not be afraid of the tumor breaking the skin.

00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:45,100
Well, in my mind, you shouldn't be afraid of the tumor breaking through the skin

00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:48,100
because the tumor is basically trying to come out.

00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:53,100
When it does break through the skin, now we have the ability to use surface killers,

00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:58,100
like salves, black salve, blood root, things like that,

00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:01,100
that can be beneficial to help kill the cancer.

00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:06,100
When it's deeper there, you can't use topicals to help kill the cancer

00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,100
because we can't get in it.

00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:16,100
However, that being said, I realize not everybody has the intestinal fortitude

00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:19,100
to have their skin break open and the cancer start coming out

00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:25,100
and have the desire to deal with it maybe weeping, it might be bleeding,

00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:29,100
and have the fear of putting on a black salve.

00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:34,100
Currently, we have another women that are doing that with great success.

00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:42,100
However, I do realize too that not every woman with breast cancer is willing to walk that walk.

00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:46,100
And that's okay, too. It doesn't mean it doesn't mean it's bad.

00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:52,100
Sometimes, if that's the case, then maybe doing some people are more comfortable

00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:56,100
with doing a mastectomy or doing some chemotherapy along with the actual things.

00:03:56,100 --> 00:04:00,100
That's okay too. Everybody's got to walk that walk and make that judgment.

00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:06,100
But I would say there can be benefit to it breaking through the skin.

00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:12,100
You just have to be ready to go through the consequences of that too.

00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:16,100
It's going to definitely make giant mishapes of your breast.

00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:19,100
There's going to be wounds that are going to heal.

00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:26,100
There's positives and negatives of that too, so we just need to understand all the aspects of that.

00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:31,100
Additionally, if my body is doing well without chemotherapy,

00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:39,100
will adding chemotherapy actually help my body's work that has already been doing?

00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:43,100
Or will it destroy all that good things that my body is doing?

00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:48,100
So will adding chemotherapy add to my body killing the cancer?

00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:53,100
Or will it kind of set me back? That's a great question.

00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:59,100
And nobody could really answer that question perfectly because there isn't a perfect answer.

00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:04,100
What your body will do may be very different than somebody else's body will do.

00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:07,100
Now, I could make the argument both ways.

00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:10,100
I could make the argument, boy, you're doing such a great job.

00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,100
Your body's killing this cancer. It's shrinking.

00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:14,100
You're having all these great results.

00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:17,100
Just stay the course. Keep doing this.

00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:21,100
And that might be right for 50% of the people.

00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:24,100
But also, I could make the argument, your body's doing great.

00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:26,100
It's killing the cancer.

00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:30,100
Let's now hit it with some harder things too, like chemotherapy.

00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:34,100
And we're going to be just going to the right direction and this is going to knock it down.

00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:38,100
And that might be perfect for 50% of the people.

00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:43,100
So you have to feel comfortable, which way God is leading you.

00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:46,100
I think you could make the argument either way.

00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:50,100
You don't know how you're about maybe if you do chemotherapy.

00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,100
It's going to knock you for a loop.

00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,100
And it's going to maybe knock it down.

00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:56,100
But then it's going to grow back faster.

00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:59,100
We just don't have those answers. Nobody has those answers.

00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,100
I can't tell you that answer.

00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:04,100
Don't listen to anybody that can give you these dogmatic answers or these instances

00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,100
because there isn't one.

00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,100
Everybody is different.

00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,100
Second part of this question.

00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:14,100
I've had one infusion and a question whether it's right for me,

00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:17,100
given how well my body has been working on the cancer without it.

00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:23,100
That's a great comment there because you have to find out if it's right for you.

00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:27,100
And the only way you know that is you have to have peace in your heart about that.

00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:31,100
And I tell people over and over again, this is how I deal with it.

00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:37,100
I believe that God, he's promised to put his desires in my heart

00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:41,100
if I seek after him with my whole heart.

00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:44,100
So that is my work in life.

00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:50,100
Is to seek after him and to be begging him to give me a desire to do that.

00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:54,100
A desire for his word and a desire for that relationship with him.

00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:59,100
That I could know, that I know, that I know what his will is for me.

00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:03,100
And that should be my main concern.

00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:07,100
That whether I should do keyboard or not, but Lord, I need to have a relationship with you

00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:12,100
close enough that I feel comfortable that I know which way you're leading me.

00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:17,100
And then I can trust wholeheartedly in you, regardless of what that is.

00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:23,100
If I believe God's leading me to do keyboard, well, then I want you to have the best attitude going in there

00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:26,100
and doing keyboard because God has sent me here to do keyboard.

00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:30,100
And he's going to have this work for me just the way he wants it to work for me.

00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:34,100
Maybe not the way I want it to work, but the way he wants it to work for me

00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:37,100
and therefore he's going to get all the glory.

00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:41,100
If he, if my desire is to seek after him and I'm seeking after him

00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:46,100
and I'm asking for him for a passion, a greater passion for him,

00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:52,100
greater knowledge for him and greater wisdom so that I can walk in that wisdom

00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:57,100
and be obedient to that wisdom, he will give that to me if that's what my heart is.

00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:59,100
And I'm going to have peace about my decision.

00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:03,100
And if my decision is to, you know, I still feel right about this.

00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,100
He will, I'm going to cancel it.

00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,100
There's nothing wrong with doing that.

00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:09,100
It doesn't mean just because you agree to he will therapy

00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:11,100
that you have to do it every three weeks.

00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:13,100
You can skip a week. You can skip a session.

00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:16,100
You can stop after one. You can stop after two.

00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:18,100
You can postpone it for six months.

00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:21,100
If you don't have an oncologist that will work with you that way,

00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:23,100
then find a different oncologist.

00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:26,100
You have to be obedient to Christ.

00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:30,100
Before you will be obedient to anybody else, okay?

00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:32,100
How do I know if I be obedient to Christ?

00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:34,100
I don't know. I want to be obedient to God.

00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:37,100
Well, then you need to seek after him first.

00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:41,100
Seek him first and all else will be given to you.

00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,100
So seek him and tell you no.

